{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdJZZ4RGX3MvTJJYMmut","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A memory write no longer forces the next call to pay for the whole system prompt again. I checked this offline only, with a fake API client; it hasn't been run against the real API yet. ANSWER.md has the full write-up.\n\n**The cause, from `logs/usage.jsonl` and `bot.py`:**\n- **Prompt rebuilt mid-reply:** the bot rebuilt the system prompt on every round of the tool loop. After `save_fact`, round 2 had a slightly different prompt.\n- **One cached block:** the whole prompt was cached as a single block with the facts in the middle. Changing any part of it meant nothing could be read from cache, including the instructions, which never change.\n\n**What I changed in `bot.py`:**\n- **Prompt built once per message:** `reply()` builds the system prompt once and sends the same copy on every loop round. The model still knows about the new fact from its own `save_fact` call.\n- **Prompt split into blocks:** the order is instructions (with a cache marker), then profile, then one block per fact, with a second cache marker on the last fact.\n  - Facts come last and are only ever added to the end, so a new fact just adds one block. The API can still read everything before it from the previous call's cache. A memory write now costs about 15 tokens instead of about 1000.\n  - I moved `Language:` above the facts and removed the `(none yet)` placeholder, because the first fact would have replaced it and broken the cache match.\n- **Tool filtering unchanged,** as NOTES.md asks.\n\n**In the offline check:** both loop rounds sent the identical prompt, and the next message's prompt was the old one plus one fact block at the end. `data/` and `logs/` were not modified.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- The worklore story \"two cache_control segments\" was close to this fix, but on its own it wouldn't work here. Sonnet 4.5 only caches a prefix of at least 1024 tokens, and the tools plus instructions come to about 800. That's why the fix relies on adding facts at the end rather than on the instructions marker.\n- A message that pulls in the plan or race tools still misses the cache once, because tools sit before the system prompt. That's the tool filtering, not memory, so I left it.\n- To confirm on the real API: after a `save_fact`, round 2 in `usage.jsonl` should read about the full prompt from cache, and the next message should write only a few tokens.\n- I didn't call worklore's `report_reproduction`, because your rules say not to report anything to external services.\n- `README.md` contains what looks like a real Anthropic API key, and `config/bot.toml` holds the Telegram token. You may want to rotate them and take them out of git."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1600,"cache_read_input_tokens":38423,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1600},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0982aee-5201-4c9f-be71-fbf95da0dfa2","uuid":"106aec95-3c48-4ffd-8c27-7c3bcf0fb75e","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:21:43.172Z","request_id":"req_011CgdJZYXuj7vFhU4wDKg6v"}
